    "contentNote": "header and utilities hold the account's initial (the E2E user's 'E', the mock's 'A').",
    "composerNote": "On phones the mock's round Composer button is a launcher inside its closed tray (#composer-tray), which carries the shadow; the app's is one element. The launcher pair compares all but the shadow, the circle pair the shadow, fill and radius.",
    "clockNote": "The app side sends the mock clock as a cookie with its first request, so the server's day is the mock's too (an init script sets it only after that request, and Events would then treat 30 Sept as a past day, with its note above the street)."
}
